      "defaultCode": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>My introduction page</title>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f8fafc; color: #1e293b; margin: 0; padding: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }\n    h1 { color: #1e3a8a; }\n    .container { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }\n    .card { width: 220px; max-width: 100%; padding: 20px; background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 14px; box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, .08); }\n    .btn { font: inherit; padding: 10px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9px; background: #2563eb; color: white; cursor: pointer; }\n    .btn:hover, .btn:focus-visible { background: #1d4ed8; }\n    .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #0f172a; outline-offset: 3px; }\n    @media (max-width: 600px) { .container { flex-direction: column; } .card { width: 100%; } }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>My introduction page</h1>\n  <main class=\"container\">\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>About me</h2><p>Hello. I am learning web development.</p></section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>Interests</h2><p>I like music and web design.</p>\n      <p id=\"interest-detail\" aria-live=\"polite\">Click the button to read more about my interests.</p>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\">More interests</button>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>My goal</h2><p>I want to build pages that my friends can use easily.</p></section>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "answerCode": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>My introduction page</title>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f8fafc; color: #1e293b; margin: 0; padding: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }\n    h1 { color: #1e3a8a; }\n    .container { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }\n    .card { width: 220px; max-width: 100%; padding: 20px; background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 14px; box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, .08); }\n    .btn { font: inherit; padding: 10px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9px; background: #2563eb; color: white; cursor: pointer; }\n    .btn:hover, .btn:focus-visible { background: #1d4ed8; }\n    .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #0f172a; outline-offset: 3px; }\n    @media (max-width: 600px) { .container { flex-direction: column; } .card { width: 100%; } }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>My introduction page</h1>\n  <main class=\"container\">\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>About me</h2><p>Hello. I am learning web development.</p></section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>Interests</h2><p>I like music and web design.</p>\n      <p id=\"interest-detail\" aria-live=\"polite\">Click the button to read more about my interests.</p>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"showInterest()\">More interests</button>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>My goal</h2><p>I want to build pages that my friends can use easily.</p></section>\n  </main>\n\n  <script>\n    function showInterest() {\n      document.getElementById(\"interest-detail\").textContent = \"I want to learn web design and build a small page about music.\";\n    }\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "lessonHtml": "\n<div class=\"info-box lesson-goal\"><strong><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-target\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Your goal</strong><p>Complete an introduction page that uses HTML, CSS, and JavaScript together.</p></div>\n<h2><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-lightbulb\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Key ideas</h2>\n<p><strong>HTML</strong> creates about, interests, and goals cards. <strong>CSS</strong> handles layout, colors, and spacing. <strong>JavaScript</strong> makes the “More interests” button work.</p>\n<p>Completion means <strong>three cards + Flexbox + readable colors and spacing + a button that changes text</strong>. Styling alone is not the whole task.</p>\n<p class=\"micro-help\">The interests button in the starting example is not connected yet. In step 3, you connect its function so the text can change.</p>\n<div class=\"problem-area\"><h3 class=\"problem-title\"><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-wrench\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Try it</h3><ol><li>Change the heading and three cards to your own introduction, interests, and goals.</li><li>Check the existing Flexbox, wrapping, and card spacing. Change one gap or color to suit your page.</li><li>Add this <code>script</code> and function just before <code>&lt;/body&gt;</code>.<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;\n  function showInterest() {\n    document.getElementById(\"interest-detail\").textContent = \"I want to build a page about music.\";\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre><p>Then use <strong>Find the part to change</strong> and replace the whole selected opening button tag with the example below. Keep the button’s text and <code>&lt;/button&gt;</code>.</p><pre><code>&lt;button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"showInterest()\"&gt;</code></pre></li><li>Read the page in wide and narrow previews and try the button.</li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"summary-box\"><strong><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-eye\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Expected result</strong><p>Three cards appear. “More interests” shows a specific sentence about your interests.</p></div>\n<p class=\"theory-callout\">Use your own goals. You can complete this project without entering real contact details.</p>\n",
      "checks": [
        "I have about, interests, and goal cards.",
        "My interests button works.",
        "I checked phone and wide layouts."
      ],
      "focusText": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\">",
      "focusLabel": "Replace the whole selected opening button tag as shown. Keep its text and closing tag.",
