      "defaultCode": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>My web page presentation</title>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f8fafc; color: #1e293b; margin: 0; padding: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }\n    h1 { color: #1e3a8a; }\n    .container { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }\n    .card { width: 220px; max-width: 100%; padding: 20px; background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 14px; box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, .08); }\n    .btn { font: inherit; padding: 10px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9px; background: #2563eb; color: white; cursor: pointer; }\n    .btn:hover, .btn:focus-visible { background: #1d4ed8; }\n    .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #0f172a; outline-offset: 3px; }\n    @media (max-width: 600px) { .container { flex-direction: column; } .card { width: 100%; } }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>My web page presentation</h1>\n  <main class=\"container\">\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>About me</h2><p>Hello. I am learning web development.</p></section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>Interests</h2><p>I like music and web design.</p>\n      <p id=\"interest-detail\" aria-live=\"polite\">Click the button to read more about my interests.</p>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"showInterest()\">More interests</button>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>My goal</h2><p>I want to build pages that my friends can use easily.</p></section>\n  </main>\n\n  <script>\n    function showInterest() {\n      document.getElementById(\"interest-detail\").textContent = \"I want to learn web design and build a small page about music.\";\n    }\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "answerCode": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>My web page presentation</title>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f8fafc; color: #1e293b; margin: 0; padding: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }\n    h1 { color: #1e3a8a; }\n    .container { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }\n    .card { width: 220px; max-width: 100%; padding: 20px; background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 14px; box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, .08); }\n    .btn { font: inherit; padding: 10px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9px; background: #2563eb; color: white; cursor: pointer; }\n    .btn:hover, .btn:focus-visible { background: #1d4ed8; }\n    .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #0f172a; outline-offset: 3px; }\n    @media (max-width: 600px) { .container { flex-direction: column; } .card { width: 100%; } }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>My web page presentation</h1>\n  <main class=\"container\">\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>About me</h2><p>Hello. I am learning web development.</p></section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>Interests</h2><p>I like music and web design.</p>\n      <p id=\"interest-detail\" aria-live=\"polite\">Click the button to read more about my interests.</p>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"showInterest()\">More interests</button>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2>My goal</h2><p>I want to build pages that my friends can use easily.</p></section>\n  </main>\n\n  <script>\n    function showInterest() {\n      document.getElementById(\"interest-detail\").textContent = \"I want to learn web design and build a small page about music.\";\n    }\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "lessonHtml": "\n<div class=\"info-box lesson-goal\"><strong><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-target\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Your goal</strong><p>Check your page and introduce it in three sentences.</p></div>\n<h2><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-lightbulb\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Key ideas</h2>\n<p>At first, this lesson opens its own example. Press <strong>Import my Lesson 13 project</strong> to bring in the Lesson 13 code saved in this browser. The original in Lesson 13 stays unchanged. If you have no saved project, write some code in Lesson 13 first.</p>\n<p>Before presenting, check the title, readable colors, narrow layout, and button. Demonstrate <strong>what changes after a click</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"problem-area\"><h3 class=\"problem-title\"><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-wrench\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Try it</h3><ol><li>Press <strong>Import my Lesson 13 project</strong> above the editor. If no project is saved, edit Lesson 13 first or practice with this lesson’s example.</li><li>Run and check the heading and cards. Click the preview button to show its action. You can also use Tab to reach the button and Enter to press it.</li><li>Prepare: “This page introduces ___. When I click ___, ___ changes. Next, I want to improve ___.”</li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"summary-box\"><strong><span class=\"lesson-icon icon-eye\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Expected result</strong><p>You can show the page and its action in 30–60 seconds and name one improvement.</p></div>\n<p class=\"theory-callout\">Review: HTML = structure, CSS = style, JavaScript = actions. This lesson’s answer is one possible presentation example.</p>\n",
      "checks": [
        "I checked my project title and content.",
        "I can demonstrate the button action.",
        "I can name one thing to improve."
      ],
      "focusText": "<h1>My web page presentation</h1>",
